// @check
// @error extern `rax` is declared `let: i64` here and `let: i32` elsewhere — one name is one host import, so every declaration of it must agree
// CONTRACT (must-error): the extern link rule applies to globals as it does to functions. Type
// and mutability are both part of the import, so `extern let` beside `extern const` of one
